  <h3>Psychographic Profile</h3>

  <p>Psychographic research indicates that the target market for StarCare is motivated by several key factors:</p>

  <div class="psychographic-box">
    <h4>Trust in the Pharmacist</h4>
    <p>Patients who know their pharmacist by name and feel comfortable asking questions are 3.2× more likely to remain loyal to a pharmacy than patients who do not (Pharmacy Loyalty Report, 2024). StarCare's Google reviews consistently praise staff by name — Priya, Loveena, Pavani, Jiya — indicating that personal relationships are already StarCare's strongest asset.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="psychographic-box">
    <h4>Convenience and Transparency</h4>
    <p>58% of patients will switch pharmacies for better convenience (Pharmacy Market Research, 2024). But "convenience" in Prosper means more than location — it means transparent pricing, clear insurance communication, and no surprises at the register. Prosper residents are affluent but highly price-aware; they will pay for quality but resent being overcharged.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="psychographic-box">
    <h4>Community Connection</h4>
    <p>Prosper residents are deeply community-oriented — 87.9% own their homes, Prosper ISD is one of the top school districts in Texas, and the town's population grew 47.9% in five years. Patients who feel connected to a pharmacy's community presence are 2.1× more likely to recommend it to others (Community Pharmacy Engagement Study, 2024).</p>
  </div>

