  <h3>Market Gap Analysis</h3>

  <p>The competitive landscape reveals three clear gaps that StarCare can exploit:</p>

  <p><strong>Gap 1: Personalized care without a loyalty system.</strong> StarCare already delivers personalized care — staff know patients by name, reviews praise individual pharmacists. But this personalization is <em>unsystematic</em>: it depends on individual staff remembering details, not on a structured retention program. A loyalty program would <em>formalize</em> what StarCare already does well, making it repeatable regardless of staff changes.</p>

  <p><strong>Gap 2: Billing transparency.</strong> StarCare's Yelp rating (2.6/5) is significantly lower than its Google rating (4.5/5), and the Yelp reviews are dominated by billing and insurance complaints. This is a <em>fixable</em> problem: a pre-fill copay confirmation system, automated prior authorization alerts, and a post-visit satisfaction survey would eliminate the #1 driver of patient attrition.</p>

  <p><strong>Gap 3: Community integration.</strong> No independent pharmacy in Prosper has a structured community engagement strategy. StarCare's "health partner" vision is aspirational — but it requires <em>visible community presence</em>: health screenings, school sponsorships, immunization clinics. Chains have loyalty programs; StarCare can have <em>community roots</em>.</p>

