  <div class="section-label">Section IV — Page 10 of 20</div>
  <h1>IV. Findings & Conclusions (continued)</h1>

  <h2>C. The SWASTIK Loyalty Framework</h2>

  <p>The six conclusions converge into a single strategic framework — <strong>Project Swastik</strong> — named for the ancient Sanskrit symbol (सवस्तिक) representing well-being, auspiciousness, and holistic health. The framework has three pillars, each addressing a specific loyalty driver identified in the research:</p>

  <div class="pillar-card">
    <h4>Pillar 1: Drishti (दृष्टि — "Vision")</h4>
    <p class="sanskrit">Vision through transparency</p>
    <p>Build trust through billing transparency and proactive communication. Before the patient picks up a prescription, they know the copay. Before insurance denies a medication, they get an alert. Before a refill is due, they get a reminder. Drishti is the <strong>foundation</strong> — without trust, no loyalty program works.</p>
    <p><strong>Key initiative:</strong> Pre-fill Copay Confirmation System + Automated Prior Auth Alerts</p>
  </div>

  <div class="pillar-card accent">
    <h4>Pillar 2: Seva (सेवा — "Service")</h4>
    <p class="sanskrit">Service through personalization</p>
    <p>Build a household-based loyalty program that rewards health engagement, not just spending. Patients earn "wellness points" for filling prescriptions on time, attending free health screenings, referring family members, and purchasing OTC products. Points redeemable for OTC discounts, free screenings, and wellness products. Seva is the <strong>engine</strong> — it drives repeat behavior and increases lifetime value.</p>
    <p><strong>Key initiative:</strong> StarCare Wellness Rewards — a household account with family profiles, wellness points, and health-focused redemption options</p>
  </div>

  <div class="pillar-card">
    <h4>Pillar 3: Milap (मिलाप — "Connection")</h4>
    <p class="sanskrit">Connection through community roots</p>
    <p>Build visible community presence through sponsorships, health screenings, and wellness workshops. StarCare becomes more than a pharmacy — it becomes a <strong>community health partner</strong>. Milap is the <strong>amplifier</strong> — it deepens emotional ties and turns patients into advocates who refer others.</p>
    <p><strong>Key initiative:</strong> StarCare Community Health Program — quarterly health screenings, school sponsorships, immunization clinics, and wellness workshops at Prosper community centers</p>
  </div>

  <h2>D. From Findings to Strategy</h2>

  <p>The strategic plan in Section V is a direct translation of these findings and conclusions. Each recommendation maps to a specific finding:</p>

