  <h1>IX. Appendix</h1>

  <h2>A. Patient Survey Instrument (Draft)</h2>

  <p>The following draft survey instrument will be used for primary data collection. Questions will be finalized after pilot testing with 10–15 patients.</p>

  <div class="appendix-box">
    <h4>Section A: Pharmacy Habits</h4>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">A1.</span> Which pharmacy(ies) do you currently use for prescriptions? (Select all that apply)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">A2.</span> How many prescriptions does your household fill per year? (0–3 / 4–7 / 8–12 / 13+)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">A3.</span> What is the primary reason you chose your current pharmacy? (Price / Location / Pharmacist relationship / Insurance / Other)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">A4.</span> How often do you purchase OTC products when you pick up a prescription? (Always / Usually / Sometimes / Rarely)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">A5.</span> Approximately how much do you spend at your pharmacy per month? (Under $25 / $25–$50 / $51–$100 / Over $100)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="appendix-box">
    <h4>Section B: Loyalty Program Awareness</h4>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">B1.</span> Are you currently enrolled in any pharmacy loyalty programs? (CVS ExtraBucks / Walmart Price Match / Costco Price Match / None)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">B2.</span> How often do you use your loyalty rewards? (Every time / Sometimes / Never)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">B3.</span> Has a loyalty program ever convinced you to switch pharmacies? (Yes / No / Not sure)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">B4.</span> On a scale of 1–5, how important are loyalty rewards when choosing a pharmacy? (1 = not important, 5 = very important)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="appendix-box">
    <h4>Section C: Loyalty Drivers (Rank by Importance)</h4>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">C1.</span> Please rank the following factors by importance when choosing a pharmacy: (1 = most important)</div>
    <div class="survey-q" style="padding-left: 1rem;">___ Low copay price &nbsp; ___ Pharmacist relationship &nbsp;___ Convenience/location</div>
    <div class="survey-q" style="padding-left: 1rem;">___ Transparent billing &nbsp;___ Free delivery &nbsp;___ Personalized health advice</div>
    <div class="survey-q" style="padding-left: 1rem;">___ Loyalty rewards &nbsp;___ Community presence &nbsp;___ Online/app tools</div>
  </div>

  <div class="appendix-box">
    <h4>Section D: Program Preferences</h4>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">D1.</span> Which of the following Wellness Rewards benefits would you value most? (Select top 3)</div>
    <div class="survey-q" style="padding-left: 1rem;">___ Free health screenings &nbsp;___ Points for OTC discounts &nbsp;___ Refill reminders</div>
    <div class="survey-q" style="padding-left: 1rem;">___ Family-wide account &nbsp;___ Referral bonuses &nbsp;___ Wellness workshop access</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">D2.</span> Would you enroll in a pharmacy loyalty program that rewards health engagement (not just spending)? (Definitely / Probably / Maybe / Probably not)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">D3.</span> How would you prefer to receive pharmacy updates? (In-person / Phone / SMS / Printed mail)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="appendix-box">
    <h4>Section E: Demographics</h4>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">E1.</span> Age range: (18–24 / 25–34 / 35–44 / 45–54 / 55–64 / 65+)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">E2.</span> Household size: (1 / 2 / 3 / 4 / 5+)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">E3.</span> Number of children in household: (0 / 1 / 2 / 3 / 4+)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">E4.</span> Annual household income: (Under $75K / $75K–$150K / Over $150K)</div>
    <div class="survey-q"><span class="q-number">E5.</span> How long have you lived in Prosper? (Under 1 year / 1–3 years / 3–5 years / 5+ years)</div>
  </div>

  <h2>B. Competitor Observation Checklist</h2>

  <div class="appendix-box">
    <h4>StarCare Pharmacy — Observation Protocol</h4>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Arrival:</strong> Signage visibility, entrance accessibility, waiting area comfort</li>
      <li><strong>Counter interaction:</strong> Greeting warmth, wait time, staff knowledge, pharmacist availability</li>
      <li><strong>Store layout:</strong> OTC section organization, seasonal display, promotional signage, checkout flow</li>
      <li><strong>Loyalty visibility:</strong> Is a loyalty program promoted? Where? How prominently?</li>
      <li><strong>Pricing transparency:</strong> Are prices visible? Is copay communicated proactively?</li>
      <li><strong>Departure:</strong> Follow-up information provided? Delivery options mentioned?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>C. Stakeholder Interview Guide</h2>

  <div class="appendix-box">
    <h4>Sample Interview Questions (Patient Version)</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>What made you choose StarCare Pharmacy over the chains nearby?</li>
      <li>What would make you consider switching pharmacies?</li>
      <li>How do you find out about new products or services at StarCare?</li>
      <li>If StarCare had a rewards program, what would make it worth your time?</li>
      <li>What does "personalized care" mean to you at a pharmacy?</li>
      <li>How important is it to you that a pharmacy is involved in the Prosper community?</li>
      <li>Would you refer StarCare to a friend? What would make you more likely to refer?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

